# amd64.pkgs — package catalogue for the native (PROF_KIND=native) live
# profiles: amd64, amd64kde, intelgnome, …
#
# Derived from this host's /var/lib/portage/world — top-level packages ONLY.
# Dependencies are deliberately absent: portage pulls them in anyway, and
# listing them would freeze today's dependency graph into the profile.
#
# FORMAT
#   # @tier <name>   opens a tier; everything until the next @tier belongs to it
#   # ...            free comment, ignored
#   <category/pkg>   one atom per line (slot deps like dev-lang/lua:5.4 are fine)
#
# A profile selects tiers with PROF_LIVE_TIERS and may append single atoms with
# PROF_LIVE_EXTRA_PKGS. Tiers are unioned in the order the profile lists them;
# xstage deduplicates. Nothing here is mandatory — @system already ships the
# real base, these are the packages that make the image useful.
#
# Sizing note: 'base portage net fs sec arch admin' lands around a 1.5 GB
# squashfs. Adding 'kde' or 'gnome' roughly doubles it; the host-* tiers and
# 'office' run to tens of GB and belong on the host, not on a live image.


